# Build output
dist/
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python virtualenvs. `node_modules`' opposite number: third-party code this
# repo neither authors nor formats. Without this, `format:check` fails on the
# JSON that ships inside installed packages (SBOMs, JSON Schemas).
**/.venv/

# Generated code — rewritten by `buf generate` / `prisma generate`, so
# formatting it only produces a diff that comes straight back on the next run.
# ESLint already skips these via the `**/generated/**` ignore in eslint.config.mjs.
**/generated/
# The Java constants `npm run java:contracts` writes. `--check` compares them
# byte for byte with the generator's output, so a formatter that rewraps them
# makes the check fail on files nobody edited.
services/api-gateway/src/main/java/com/synapsedesk/gateway/common/contracts/

# Lockfiles. npm owns their formatting and rewrites them wholesale on every
# install; prettier reformatting one produces a diff that comes straight back,
# and a `format:check` that fails after `npm i` teaches people to skip the
# gate. Excluded HERE rather than by shaping the glob around them, so the
# coverage check in `ci-contract.spec.ts` — which reads from the files toward
# the config — sees a deliberate exclusion instead of an uncovered file.
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json

# Maven build output — `dist/`'s opposite number for the Java module, and it
# only became load-bearing when `*.java`/`*.xml` entered the format globs.
# Measured: ~470 generated sources under `target/generated-sources` (OpenAPI
# models, protobuf and grpc stubs) plus surefire's XML reports, every one of
# them rewritten by `./mvnw`. `**/generated/` above does NOT cover them — the
# path component is `generated-sources`, not `generated` — and prettier does not
# read `.gitignore`, so `services/api-gateway/.gitignore` does not reach here.
target/

# pytest's JUnit report, written by `npm run test:py -- --junitxml=pytest.xml`.
# Generated, and present on any machine that has run the Python suite once.
**/pytest.xml

